.TH AD-TUNE 1 "2026-08-20" "diffvim 2.0" "diffvim tuning"
.SH NAME
ad_tune \- interactive workbench for tuning ad postprocessing and pacing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_tune
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIoldfile newfile\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_tune
provides a menu-driven interface for testing diffvim options on short
files. It can stream ops to an animator running in another terminal
via file descriptor 5 or named pipes, enabling side-by-side comparison
of different option combinations.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-workdir \ DIR
Directory for intermediate files (default: temp dir)
.TP
.BI \-\-stream \ FD
Stream ops to file descriptor FD (e.g., 5)
.TP
.BI \-\-stream-pipe \ PIPE
Stream ops to a named pipe
.TP
.B \-\-tmux
Run the animator in a tmux split pane
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help and exit
.SH "INTERACTIVE COMMANDS"
.TP
.B r
Run the full pipeline + animate
.TP
.B p
Show post-processed ops in less
.TP
.B t
Show timed ops in less
.TP
.B v
Generate per-op HTML visualization
.TP
.B m
Run minimal test suite
.TP
.B b
Generate debug bundle (tar.gz with user description)
.TP
.B e / E
Edit old / new file
.TP
.B s
Swap old and new files
.TP
.B d
Diff old and new files
.TP
.B +
Add a setting via fzf (or manual input)
.TP
.B c
Clear all changes
.TP
.B S / L
Save / load settings
.TP
.B 1-9
Quick toggle settings
.TP
.B q
Quit
.SH "STREAMING TO AN ANIMATOR"
Multiple ad_tune instances can stream ops to a single animator:
.PP
.nf
# Terminal 1: named pipe
mkfifo /tmp/dv_pipe
ad_tune --stream-pipe /tmp/dv_pipe old1.txt new1.txt

# Terminal 2: animator reads from pipe
ad old1.txt < /tmp/dv_pipe

# Terminal 3: another ad_tune with different options
ad_tune --stream-pipe /tmp/dv_pipe2 old2.txt new2.txt
.fi
.SH "DEBUG BUNDLE"
Pressing
.B b
generates a tar.gz containing:
.IP \(bu 2
old.txt, new.txt
.IP \(bu 2
raw.txt, post.txt, timed.txt, decorated.txt
.IP \(bu 2
settings.conf
.IP \(bu 2
system_info.txt
.IP \(bu 2
description.txt (typed by the user)
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR diffvim (1),
.BR ad_layer_highlight (1),
.BR ad (1)
